                                                    <div class="eventWrapper ew4">
                                                        
                                                            <div class="followLine"></div>
                                                        
                                                        
                                                        <div class="eventContent">
                                                            <!-- <img src="https://download.snec.org.cn/SNEC/img/2026/04/24//AI论坛-92466945.jpg" data-title="3rd Summit on AI + Energy Digitalization for the New Power Systems" data-intro="&lt;p&gt;Closely aligned with the strategic directions for energy development outlined in China&amp;rsquo;s 15th Five-Year Plan, this Forum focuses on key objectives such as accelerating the construction of a new energy system, enhancing renewable energy supply capabilities, and advancing the development of a next-generation power system. Centered on the theme of &amp;ldquo;Power Intelligent Agents Reshaping the Intelligent Core and Standards Ecosystem of the Next-Generation Power System,&amp;rdquo; this Forum aims to drive the evolution of power systems toward greater intelligence, autonomy, and coordination through the dual engines of intelligent agent technologies and standardized frameworks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Building on this central theme, this Forum is structured around three core thematic tracks. The first focuses on the technological core, with in-depth discussions on algorithmic breakthroughs and architectural innovation in power intelligent agents, covering core technology R&amp;amp;D, algorithm adaptation, and domestic substitution and &amp;nbsp;providing technical support for industry applications and standards development. The second track emphasizes scenario-based deployment, examining integration pathways and value creation of power intelligent agents across diverse real-world applications, and validating their commercial viability through practical case studies. The third track addresses the standards framework, concentrating on alignment between domestic and international standards as well as mechanisms for industry-wide collaboration, with the goal of promoting the standardized development of power intelligent agents and fostering a shared industrial ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This Forum will convene dedicated thematic workshops and to release the abridged version of the New-Type Power System: Intelligent Agent Architecture, Technologies, and Applications Research Report. Representatives from government, industry, academia, research institutions, and the financial sector will be widely invited to participate, creating a cross-disciplinary platform for in-depth exchange and collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
" alt="https://download.snec.org.cn/SNEC/img/2026/04/24//AI论坛-92466945.jpg"/> -->
                                                            <div class="eventImg" style="background-image: url('https://download.snec.org.cn/SNEC/img/2026/04/24//AI论坛-92466945.jpg');" data-src="https://download.snec.org.cn/SNEC/img/2026/04/24//AI论坛-92466945.jpg" data-title="3rd Summit on AI + Energy Digitalization for the New Power Systems" data-intro="&lt;p&gt;Closely aligned with the strategic directions for energy development outlined in China&amp;rsquo;s 15th Five-Year Plan, this Forum focuses on key objectives such as accelerating the construction of a new energy system, enhancing renewable energy supply capabilities, and advancing the development of a next-generation power system. Centered on the theme of &amp;ldquo;Power Intelligent Agents Reshaping the Intelligent Core and Standards Ecosystem of the Next-Generation Power System,&amp;rdquo; this Forum aims to drive the evolution of power systems toward greater intelligence, autonomy, and coordination through the dual engines of intelligent agent technologies and standardized frameworks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Building on this central theme, this Forum is structured around three core thematic tracks. The first focuses on the technological core, with in-depth discussions on algorithmic breakthroughs and architectural innovation in power intelligent agents, covering core technology R&amp;amp;D, algorithm adaptation, and domestic substitution and &amp;nbsp;providing technical support for industry applications and standards development. The second track emphasizes scenario-based deployment, examining integration pathways and value creation of power intelligent agents across diverse real-world applications, and validating their commercial viability through practical case studies. The third track addresses the standards framework, concentrating on alignment between domestic and international standards as well as mechanisms for industry-wide collaboration, with the goal of promoting the standardized development of power intelligent agents and fostering a shared industrial ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This Forum will convene dedicated thematic workshops and to release the abridged version of the New-Type Power System: Intelligent Agent Architecture, Technologies, and Applications Research Report. Representatives from government, industry, academia, research institutions, and the financial sector will be widely invited to participate, creating a cross-disciplinary platform for in-depth exchange and collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
"></div>
